\description{
Visibility and interrupt checks

Test that a function with explicit -> () return is invisible in R.

Test that returning None from Option<()> produces an R error.

Test that returning Some(()) from Option<()> is invisible in R.

Test that returning Ok(()) from Result<(), ()> is invisible in R.

Test that Result Err(()) returns NULL in R, Ok returns doubled value.

Test that #miniextendr(invisible) forces an i32 return to be invisible in R.

Test that #miniextendr(visible) forces a unit return to be visible in R.

Test that \verb{#[miniextendr(check_interrupt)]} checks for user interrupts before execution.

Test \code{unwrap_in_r}: the \code{Result} is converted to \code{list(error = ...)} on the R side instead of raising a condition.

\verb{Invisible<i32>}: the value is returned invisibly.

\verb{Invisible<()>}: the explicit spelling of the unit default.

\verb{Visible<()>}: a visible \code{NULL}.

The marker is transparent to \code{Option} handling: a bare function's \verb{Option<i32>} \code{None} is \code{NA}, as without the marker.

A marker and an agreeing attribute.
}
